        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Islamic Caliphates &amp; Middle East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Yarmuk</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">15 to 20 August 636, six days of fighting; some accounts say the battle lasted a day</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The plain east of Wadi-ur-Ruqqad, south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a> and east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-galilee">Sea of Galilee</a>, near the Yarmuk River on what is now the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and Jordan</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-ubayda-ibn-al-jarrah">Abu Ubayda</a>, who handed command to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a>, with 36,000 to 40,000 men in most early accounts; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> under the field commander Vahan, with 60,000 to 70,000 in most early accounts, though modern estimates run from 15,000 to 20,000 up to 80,000 to 100,000 or more</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Byzantine army was routed on the sixth day. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid</a> then entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
